  message: "Done in PR #2176 (commit a0fb850d61). Measured before choosing, on repositories that are not hypergumbo; scripts and results in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/papup_additional_files_ranking_11132026.\n(1) README LINKS IN DOCUMENT ORDER: KEPT. 444 repositories: ordering the linked files by the overview order instead leaves the first eight Additional Files the same set in 392; an architecture-named document is among them in 75 of 160 repositories against 73. It does change which linked file comes second (a process file in 76 repositories against 98). The first README link is a community, licence, change-log or install page in 115 of 248 repositories with links. Which file a README links first is the author's to change (for this repository that is docs/INTEL_MAC.md: WI-zodif).\n(2a) THE OVERVIEW ORDER PUT PROCESS FILES FIRST (the question left open by measurement 0033). With the file name as the outside label, 1.3 of its first three files were process files. Now a file named as a process file (contributing guide, code of conduct, security policy, licence, change log; whole conventional names, documents only) comes after every other file of its role. First eight Additional Files, 444 repositories (89 held out): process files 1.7 -> 0.7 a repository (1.8 -> 0.6); README-linked files 1.6 -> 1.6; the file after the README is a process file in 98 repositories, was 172. An architecture-named document is among the eight in 73 of 160, was 66, and in 15 of 30 either way on the held-out split: the rule frees a place, it does not find the design document.\n(2b) THE CENTRALITY LIST REWARDED LISTS OF NAMES. On alertmanager, kserve, killbill and prometheus, 9, 1, 13 and 9 of its first 15 files were not documentation (buf.gen.yaml, tsconfig.json, stylesheets, XML test configs). It now holds documentation files that mention at least one central symbol.\n(3) THE CONTENT RULE CUT THE FIRST FILE HARDEST. At 8k: alertmanager's README was printed as 262 tokens and its 3,665-token openapi.yaml whole; this repository's README as 469 and docs/INTEL_MAC.md whole. A file that does not fit is now cut to its harmonic share by position (ADR-0005). truncate_to_tokens no longer takes a \"## \" line inside a fenced code block for a section header (the README was cut inside its own example), and no longer returns an over-long preamble whole.\nRENDERED, with source, before -> after (first eight Additional Files; files printed with tokens, * = cut):\n  alertmanager 8k: left the first eight: buf.gen.yaml, CHANGELOG.md, ui/mantine-ui/index.html, SECURITY.md; entered: docs/alertmanager.md, examples/ha/tls/README.md, docs/alerts_api.md, docs/notifications.md. Printed: README.md 262*, api/v2/openapi.yaml 3665 -> README.md 609*, api/v2/openapi.yaml 123*, RELEASE.md 560.\n  kserve 8k: left: SECURITY.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md; entered: docs/MULTIMODELSERVING_GUIDE.md, qpext/README.md, docs/PRESENTATIONS.md.\n  killbill 8k: left: two stylesheets and an XML test config; entered: beatrix/pom.xml, account/pom.xml, invoice/pom.xml (killbill has three documentation files in all, so the places go to build files).\n  prometheus 8k: left: CHANGELOG.md; entered: discovery/README.md.\n  this repository 8k: left: CONTRIBUTING.md and the two self-catalogue YAMLs; entered: packages/hypergumbo-core/README.md, ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md, packages/hypergumbo-lang-scip-python/README.md. Printed: README.md 469*, docs/INTEL_MAC.md 1172 -> README.md 1141*.\nThe 32k lists moved the same files. What each change moved: process files leaving are (2a); data, stylesheet and config files leaving are (2b); the README sizes are (3).\nSEEN IN THESE RENDERINGS AND NOT FIXED: a file with few blank lines and no \"## \" headings is cut at its last early paragraph break (alertmanager's openapi.yaml: 123 tokens), far under its share. ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md entering this repository's first eight shows that \"not a process file, at the root\" is a weak reason to be shown.\nMutations: 18 turned a test red; one more showed a clause that could change no result, which was removed. (The commit message says nineteen.)\nNOT DONE, to be filed: the centrality score is mentions per byte, so among documents a short sample README outranks a long design document (prometheus: storage/remote/azuread/README.md first); nothing here reads what a document says about the code, and an architecture-named document is still outside the first eight in more than half of the repositories that have one (87 of 160)."  # dd8c
